WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.114 --> 00:00:01.372
- The world wants to know

00:00:01.372 --> 00:00:03.113
what it's like to date Terry Crews

00:00:03.113 --> 00:00:06.799
and the world needs somebody
to be their romantic icon

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:08.393
and I am that person.

00:00:08.393 --> 00:00:10.893
(light music)

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.801
Thank you again so much for meeting me

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:15.863
on such short notice.

00:00:15.863 --> 00:00:17.418
- Oh yeah, you got it.

00:00:17.418 --> 00:00:21.133
I met Keith for the first time today.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:24.152
He's, you know, a pretty nice guy.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:24.985
Yeah.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.301
Oh, that's all I need.

00:00:28.301 --> 00:00:30.650
I don't want to get tipsy.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.483
- [Waiter] For you?
- I'm gonna have

00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:32.316
a little more.

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:34.203
I just hope that he and I hit it off

00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:35.844
and we have some things to talk about.

00:00:35.844 --> 00:00:39.980
To the most handsome date I've ever had.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.813
- Yeah.

00:00:41.848 --> 00:00:42.681
- Cheers.

00:00:42.681 --> 00:00:43.613
What's the real Terry like?

00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:45.537
- I'm a painter, I'm an artist.

00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:48.027
I've designed furniture.

00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:48.928
Got a lot of that kind of--

00:00:48.928 --> 00:00:49.909
- Terry.

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:52.492
- I enjoy going for new things.

00:00:54.735 --> 00:00:56.860
I have a philosophy on life

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.938
where the key to success
is doing what you want

00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:02.691
and if it's not what you want,

00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:05.675
are you really successful?

00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:07.223
You got to understand with me

00:01:07.223 --> 00:01:09.635
is that I was in the art world

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:13.307
and sports world at the same
time and I saw no difference.

00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:14.140
- Really?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.312
- When I got cut from football teams,

00:01:15.312 --> 00:01:17.286
I was on six teams in seven years.

00:01:17.286 --> 00:01:18.886
When I played in the NFL,

00:01:18.886 --> 00:01:22.215
I would go back in the locker
room and ask my teammates

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.378
if they wanted portraits painted of them

00:01:24.378 --> 00:01:25.726
and that's how I survived.

00:01:25.726 --> 00:01:29.559
- There's no reality
where you would paint me?

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:32.180
Let's move on.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.122
- Okay, alright.

00:01:33.122 --> 00:01:35.819
- I thought it would be nice if

00:01:35.819 --> 00:01:38.104
we share some chocolate.

00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:40.349
I don't know if it would be too crazy

00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:42.599
if we maybe fed each other.

00:01:44.641 --> 00:01:45.888
Why don't you feed me first?

00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:48.393
- We had been going at a real nice pace

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:50.171
and then it ramped up to like 100.

00:01:50.171 --> 00:01:52.004
I was kinda like whoa.

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:54.883
You're touching the chocolate.

00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:59.499
- Obviously, when you have
the body that Terry has,

00:01:59.499 --> 00:02:01.338
it comes with a little
bit of machismo, right?

00:02:01.338 --> 00:02:02.326
You don't want to show

00:02:02.326 --> 00:02:05.226
that just anybody can
feed you a chocolate.

00:02:05.226 --> 00:02:07.795
- Just, yeah, I'm gonna
try a piece of that.

00:02:07.795 --> 00:02:08.790
- I would love giving this to you.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.850
I would love to take this to you.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.683
- Can I have a bite?
- [Keith] Of course.

00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:11.830
- I want to just try it.
- Yeah yeah.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.580
I fed him like a man.

00:02:17.606 --> 00:02:18.544
- That's pretty good.

00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:19.850
- Yeah.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.288
- Pretty good.

00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:22.264
Okay.

00:02:22.264 --> 00:02:24.021
- It was something.

00:02:24.021 --> 00:02:24.854
You know?

00:02:24.854 --> 00:02:26.715
What is next for you?

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:28.066
You have Brooklyn Nine-Nine.

00:02:28.066 --> 00:02:29.096
It's doing great.

00:02:29.096 --> 00:02:30.068
- It's awesome, man.

00:02:30.068 --> 00:02:32.682
- You're an artist, you're
a painter, you're an actor.

00:02:32.682 --> 00:02:33.515
What else?

00:02:33.515 --> 00:02:34.354
- You know what?

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.992
I never thought I'd be an actor ever

00:02:37.992 --> 00:02:42.156
but I also am leaving
space for something else.

00:02:42.156 --> 00:02:43.911
I don't know what's coming.

00:02:43.911 --> 00:02:47.994
One dream I have and this
is no joke, I'm so serious.

00:02:47.994 --> 00:02:49.829
I want to farm.

00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:50.989
I'm not even kidding.

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:51.889
I want my own--

00:02:51.889 --> 00:02:53.465
- What do you want to farm, Terry?

00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:55.019
- I'm going to have a farm.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:57.179
- What kind of plants,
what kind of animals?

00:02:57.179 --> 00:02:58.284
- I'm going to have everything.

00:02:58.284 --> 00:02:59.795
I mean, the horses, chickens.

00:02:59.795 --> 00:03:01.883
- That's irresponsible,
it's hard to raise them all.

00:03:01.883 --> 00:03:03.271
You should pick--

00:03:03.271 --> 00:03:05.271
- And then I'm gonna have
to hire a bunch of people.

00:03:05.271 --> 00:03:07.369
- Yeah, okay, now you're
good, that's it, that'll work.

00:03:07.369 --> 00:03:09.924
- You understand what I mean?

00:03:09.924 --> 00:03:12.443
- I tell you, if you don't
have shepherding experience--

00:03:12.443 --> 00:03:13.973
- I have an app.

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:15.822
No, but I would have an app
so I could watch the farm.

00:03:15.822 --> 00:03:18.605
- Yeah like a little watering
that you could water.

00:03:18.605 --> 00:03:20.393
- I would make it totally automated.

00:03:20.393 --> 00:03:21.452
- Like a cyber farm.

00:03:21.452 --> 00:03:24.433
- It'd be a cyber farm, exactly, exactly

00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:27.336
because I probably couldn't
be there all the time

00:03:27.336 --> 00:03:28.290
but I would have a staff there.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.784
- You're in too much demand.

00:03:29.784 --> 00:03:31.448
I'm so lucky to have this time

00:03:31.448 --> 00:03:33.686
because I think everybody
kinda wants a piece of you.

00:03:33.686 --> 00:03:35.160
- Keith.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.341
You're warming me up here, man.

00:03:37.341 --> 00:03:38.387
You know what?

00:03:38.387 --> 00:03:40.685
At first, I was like wow.

00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:42.790
You know just what to say.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:43.860
Okay, woo.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.446
Oh, wow.

00:03:45.446 --> 00:03:46.528
Wow.

00:03:46.528 --> 00:03:50.028
- I have one more little surprise for you.

00:03:51.247 --> 00:03:52.080
- Aw.

00:03:53.735 --> 00:03:55.205
Thank you, Keith.

00:03:55.205 --> 00:03:58.442
- I know that I don't
actually have a firm place

00:03:58.442 --> 00:03:59.827
in your family in your future.

00:03:59.827 --> 00:04:01.067
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.443
You can come home, we can hang out.

00:04:02.443 --> 00:04:03.590
It's all good, man.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.060
- Maybe Thanksgiving.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:05.918
- Maybe not Thanksgiving.

00:04:05.918 --> 00:04:07.590
- I can brine the hell out of a turkey.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.126
- No, it would kinda like an off day.

00:04:11.126 --> 00:04:12.610
And I just straight out had to say no.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.019
I just had to bust that bubble right away.

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:17.143
It was getting, the bubble
was getting bubblicious.

00:04:17.143 --> 00:04:18.570
- To your future, Terry.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.237
- Thank you and to yours, Keith.

00:04:23.446 --> 00:04:25.894
That's good, alright, thank you.

00:04:25.894 --> 00:04:28.727
Ah, this is really really awesome.

00:04:32.727 --> 00:04:33.560
- Could we hug?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.279
- Like a one arm hug?

00:04:35.279 --> 00:04:36.908
- Gosh, I'd love a two armed one.

00:04:36.908 --> 00:04:38.744
- You know, it's funny 'cause--

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.664
- We can keep our
pelvises really far apart.

00:04:41.664 --> 00:04:43.895
- Let's just do the one arm.

00:04:43.895 --> 00:04:44.859
- That's what I wanted.

00:04:44.859 --> 00:04:47.106
That's the kind of hug I wanted.

00:04:47.106 --> 00:04:47.939
- Yeah.

00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:48.939
- That's what I wanted.

00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:51.102
- One and.
- There we go.

00:04:51.102 --> 00:04:53.577
Look at that, it feels the same.

00:04:53.577 --> 00:04:54.410
Feels the same.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.526
- You smell so good too.

00:04:55.526 --> 00:04:57.036
- Thank you.
- You smell so good.

00:04:57.036 --> 00:04:59.972
I went into this date
with a little bit of doubt

00:04:59.972 --> 00:05:03.055
of where I would fall in Terry's life

00:05:03.938 --> 00:05:06.909
and I think he might have
fallen a little bit for me.

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:08.992
- You are a great person.

00:05:14.496 --> 00:05:18.060
Would I ever go on
another date with Keith?

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.950
If I want to be on Buzzfeed again, yeah.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.579
Yeah, I'd do it.

00:05:23.579 --> 00:05:24.477
- Oh, don't forget your flowers.

00:05:24.477 --> 00:05:26.651
- Oh no, yeah, that's for the family.

00:05:26.651 --> 00:05:28.117
Thank you very much.

00:05:28.117 --> 00:05:28.950
Thank you.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.299
- Thanks.

00:05:30.299 --> 00:05:33.155
I'll handle it, I'll handle
